---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import JsonLd from '@/components/JsonLd.astro';
import { Badge } from '@/components/ui/badge';
import { buttonVariants } from '@/components/ui/button';
import { SITE, urls, EVIDENCE, REPO } from '@/config';
import { getJobs, getBots } from '@/lib/data';
import { breadcrumbs } from '@/lib/seo';

const [jobs, bots] = await Promise.all([getJobs(), getBots()]);
const verified = bots.filter((b) => b.evidenceLevel === 'link-verified').length;
const open = jobs.filter((j) => j.status === 'open').length;
const bothCatalogues = bots.filter((b) => (b.listings ?? []).length > 1).length;
const creators = new Set(bots.map((b) => b.creator.handle ?? b.creator.name)).size;

const stats = [
  { n: bots.length, label: 'bots on file' },
  { n: verified, label: 'listings reconciled' },
  { n: bothCatalogues, label: 'on both catalogues' },
  { n: creators, label: 'creators credited' },
];
---

<Base
  title="Methodology — how listings are gathered, checked and ranked"
  description="How Bot Jobs gathers Grok Bots from public catalogues, reconciles each listing against the official x.ai page, ranks candidates against a job, and what our evidence labels do and do not claim."
  canonical="/methodology"
>
  <JsonLd data={breadcrumbs([{ name: 'Methodology', path: '/methodology' }])} />

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-12 pb-20 sm:px-6 sm:pt-16">
    <p class="eyebrow text-muted-foreground">How this works</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-[2.25rem] leading-[1.02] sm:text-5xl">
      What we <span class="marker">check</span>, and what we don't
    </h1>
    <p class="prose-editorial mt-5">
      Bot Jobs is a directory of things people get Grok Bot to do. This page explains where the
      listings come from, what each evidence label means, how candidates are ranked, and — the
      part most directories leave out — the limits of all of it.
    </p>

    <dl class="border-border mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 gap-px border-y sm:grid-cols-4">
      {
        stats.map(({ n, label }) => (
          <div class="py-4">
            <dt class="font-display text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">{n}</dt>
            <dd class="eyebrow text-muted-foreground mt-1">{label}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl">Where listings come from</h2>
    <div class="prose-editorial mt-3 space-y-4">
      <p>
        Bots are ingested from the public catalogues that publish machine-readable APIs —
        currently <strong>grokbot.dev</strong> and <strong>bot.store</strong> — using their
        documented endpoints rather than scraping. Every record names the catalogue it was found
        in and links to it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Both catalogues are read, which is unusual: none of the directories in this space index
        each other. {bothCatalogues} of our records appear on both, and the rest exist on only one
        — so the union is more complete than either source alone.
      </p>
      <p>
        We take facts and nothing else: the official share URL, the creator, the originating post,
        tags. We never take a catalogue's write-up. Descriptions on this site are ours, written
        from the creator's own official listing, and a record cannot be published until somebody
        has written one.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl">What the evidence labels mean</h2>
    <p class="prose-editorial mt-3">
      Three levels. They answer different questions, and the top one is narrower than it sounds.
    </p>
    <dl class="rule-list border-ink mt-4 rounded-lg border-[1.5px]">
      {
        (Object.keys(EVIDENCE) as Array<keyof typeof EVIDENCE>).map((level) => (
          <div class="p-4 sm:px-5">
            <dt class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
              <Badge variant={level}>
                <span class="size-1.5 rounded-full bg-current" aria-hidden="true" />
                {EVIDENCE[level].label}
              </Badge>
            </dt>
            <dd class="text-muted-foreground mt-2 text-sm/relaxed">{EVIDENCE[level].blurb}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>

    <div class="outlined bg-card mt-6 rounded-lg p-5">
      <h3 class="text-lg">The limit, stated plainly</h3>
      <p class="prose-editorial mt-2 text-sm">
        <strong>“References checked” does not mean we ran the bot.</strong> It means we fetched
        its official x.ai page, confirmed it resolves, and captured what xAI says about it. We
        have not watched any of these bots work. If you repeat something from this site, repeat
        that distinction with it — a checked listing is not a tested bot, and we would rather be
        useful than impressive.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl">Why reconciliation matters</h2>
    <div class="prose-editorial mt-3 space-y-4">
      <p>
        Every listing is checked against the official x.ai page rather than trusted from the
        catalogue. That is not a formality. Catalogues disagree with the source of truth: one bot
        is listed elsewhere as “Forge (dev factory)” while xAI calls it “Forge by Daniel”, and
        dozens more differ in the same way.
      </p>
      <p>
        More usefully, it catches bots that no longer exist. <strong>We have found install links
        that are dead while other directories still list them as live.</strong> A directory whose
        whole promise is “here is a bot you can add” is worth nothing if the link 404s, so the
        check runs weekly and a bot that fails three times in a row is unpublished.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl">How candidates are ranked</h2>
    <div class="prose-editorial mt-3 space-y-4">
      <p>
        A job page shows the bots we would actually put forward for that job, best fit first, each
        with a stated reason and its honest caveat. Ranking is comparative — candidates are
        assessed against each other for a specific job, not scored in isolation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Fit scores are <strong>our editorial judgement</strong>. They are not user ratings, and
        there are no ratings or reviews anywhere on this site, because we have no users to collect
        them from. Inventing them would be the easiest way to look authoritative and the fastest
        way to stop being trustworthy.
      </p>
      <p>
        Rejection is the default. Most bots fit most jobs badly, and a directory that maps
        everything to something has thrown away the only reason to read it. {open} jobs currently
        have no candidate at all and are listed as <a href={urls.openJobs()} class="underline underline-offset-2">open</a>
        rather than filled with something that does not do the work.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl">What we will not do</h2>
    <ul class="prose-editorial mt-3 space-y-2">
      <li>— Reproduce template contents, prompt bodies or reconstructed configuration. The
        official share link is the only install route and it belongs to the creator.</li>
      <li>— Republish another directory's description as our own.</li>
      <li>— Show star ratings or review counts we did not collect.</li>
      <li>— Require a link back, or make inclusion conditional on anything.</li>
      <li>— Argue about removals. Ask and it goes, within 48 hours.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl">Check it yourself</h2>
    <p class="prose-editorial mt-3">
      Every record is a file in a public repository, so the data, its history and every correction
      are readable without asking us. The datasets are also available as JSON.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2.5">
      <a href={REPO} rel="noopener" class={buttonVariants({ size: 'sm' })}>Read the records</a>
      <a href="/api/jobs.json" class={buttonVariants({ variant: 'secondary', size: 'sm' })}>jobs.json</a>
      <a href="/api/bots.json" class={buttonVariants({ variant: 'secondary', size: 'sm' })}>bots.json</a>
      <a href="/llms.txt" class={buttonVariants({ variant: 'secondary', size: 'sm' })}>llms.txt</a>
    </div>

    <p class="text-muted-foreground border-border mt-10 border-t pt-6 text-xs leading-relaxed">
      Corrections and removals: <a href={urls.report('')} class="underline underline-offset-2">{SITE.domain}/report</a>.
      Independent project, not affiliated with or endorsed by xAI.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
